rst four roots are k+4 and k+16, whose sum must be -108, so k=-64. These are P's roots -60 and -48, giving P=(x+54)^2-36. The minima sum to -64-36=-100; these forms also produce the stated roots of Q(P(x)).","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2010_AMC_12B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_032"],"id":"solution:symmetric-preimages:da8031b8c9dc","label":"Paired roots and symmetry","methodDirectNodeIds":{"symmetric-preimages":["cnm_231","math:polynomial-remainder-factor","cnm_233","cnm_235"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_231","math:polynomial-remainder-factor","cnm_233","cnm_235","cnm_032"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_032","cnm_146"],"id":"solution:composition-coefficients:da8031b8c9dc","label":"Compare coefficients of the compositions","methodDirectNodeIds":{"composition-coefficients":["math:polynomial-roots-coefficients","math:completing-square-expression","cnm_233","cnm_235"]},"nodeIds":["math:polynomial-roots-coefficients","math:completing-square-expression","cnm_233","cnm_235","cnm_032","cnm_146"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, k=3","reason":"Since c=-a-b, f(7)=6(8a+b)=54 and f(8)=7(9a+b)=77. Thus a=2, b=-7, c=5. Consequently f(100)=19305, which lies strictly between 15000 and 20000, so k=3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2011_AMC_12A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_196","cnm_p153","cnm_042"],"id":"use-integral-evaluations","label":"Use divisibility to determine the evaluations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"use-integral-evaluations":["cnm_233","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_089","cnm_090"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_233","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_089","cnm_090","cnm_196","cnm_p153","cnm_042"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, -3.","reason":"y1=a+b+c and y2=a-b+c,